course: dictionary
lesson: 8138
title: Reporters and the news
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A reporter is a person whose job is to find out news and tell it to other people, in a newspaper, on television, on the radio or online. «A reporter finds out what happened and tells the public.» The word gives you the clue: a reporter reports, which means tells about something.
explain: Good reporters check their facts before they write or speak. «Good reporters report facts, not rumours.» A rumour is an idea that people pass on without knowing if it is true. Ask yourself: is this a fact I can check, or just something I heard?
explain: Reporters do not always work on the news. In school, the group «reporter» tells the class what their group found out. Anyone who tells others what happened can act like a reporter, but a real reporter always checks the facts first.
fact: A reporter is a person who finds out news and tells it to others.
fact: Reporters can work for newspapers, television, radio or online news.
fact: «News reporter», «TV reporter» and «sports reporter» are all kinds of reporter.
fact: «Anonymous» means without giving your name, so «anonymous reporting» is telling something without saying who you are.
fact: Reporters should check what they say carefully, because a false story can spread very fast.
exercise: «A reporter finds out what happened and tells the public.» What is a reporter's job? | To cook food in a restaurant | To mend roads and bridges | To sing songs on the stage | *To find out news and tell it to others
exercise: «Good reporters report facts, not rumours.» What should a good reporter tell people? | Guesses about what might happen | *Facts that have been checked | Rumours they heard in the playground | Stories they made up
exercise: In school, what does the group «reporter» do? | Sits quietly at the back | *Tells the class what the group found out | Writes the homework for the teacher | Hands out the books
test: The word «anonymous» in «anonymous reporting» means telling something without giving what? | Your address | *Your name | Your favourite colour | Your age
test: Why should a reporter check carefully what an anonymous source says? | To make the news more exciting | Because anonymous sources are always right | To make the story longer | *Because it might not be true
exam: What is a good check for a reporter before sharing news? | *Check the facts before you tell anyone | Share it because lots of people said it | Tell the story as loudly as you can | Believe the first thing you hear
